{"The Lithuanian OTP setup message was replaced with Italian text, causing users running the account console in lt locale to see the wrong language": 0.9903252124786377, "The verifier plugin only declares the sanitizer artifact but is missing the OWASP shim artifacts (java8-shim and java10-shim), which can cause the goal to fail with a missing shim class": 0.7237890362739563, "The verifier opens a computed English sibling for every messages_*.properties file and throws an unchecked exception when it is absent, causing verify-theme to abort with a stack trace instead of returning collected validation errors": 0.9629288911819458, "The sanitizer output is compared byte-for-byte with the original value, causing allowed markup like <br /> to be reported as illegal HTML when the sanitizer canonicalizes it": 0.7263994812965393, "The account UI resource uses Java MessageFormat choice string syntax but is rendered by the JS message layer which expects {{0}} placeholders, causing the format string to be shown literally to users": 0.6542184948921204, "The admin UI resource uses {2,choice,...} syntax but is consumed by the JS message layer which expects {{0}} interpolation form, causing the text to be rendered literally in the admin console": 0.7766651511192322}